diag(min14): name every kernel_bootstrap phase on screen

min13h40: arm_init finishes (blocks 30-40 all visible) and the reset happens in machine_startup / kernel_bootstrap. kernel_bootstrap announces each phase with kernel_bootstrap_log() -> kernel_debug_string_early(). Hook it: after sweet_early_phase_begin() (end of arm_init) each call draws a coloured block at slot 41+n of the x=1300 column and writes the phase name, 16x32 px per character, to its left; herostop=N freezes after block N (up to 76). Drawing only; the one line in bsd/kern/kdebug.c is outside D-0043's file allowlist and needs the Director's extension before an image with it is written.

